Subject: [PATCH] NaSta: a query names up to 64 stations per channel

Apply to both ccsp-one-wifi and ccsp-one-wifi-libwebconfig, after 0030.
A native agent measured at most eight unassociated stations per channel
per query, so an external optimizer needed one serialized controller
query per eight stations: about 160 queries (90 s) for one round of the
fifty-client room. The controller already accepts 64 (EM_MAX_UNASSOC_STA)
and truncates responses beyond it; the response bound is now that
number, smaller than the previous product of the three limits.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/include/wifi_base.h
+++ b/include/wifi_base.h
@@ -540,8 +540,10 @@
 /* Unassociated STA (NaSta) query/response structures */
 #define MAX_NASTA_OPCLASS_ENTRIES   8
 #define MAX_NASTA_CHANNELS          8
-#define MAX_NASTA_STA_PER_CHANNEL   8
-#define MAX_NASTA_RESPONSE_STAS     (MAX_NASTA_OPCLASS_ENTRIES * MAX_NASTA_CHANNELS * MAX_NASTA_STA_PER_CHANNEL)
+/* One query may name as many stations on a channel as the controller accepts
+ * (EM_MAX_UNASSOC_STA, 64); the response carries at most that many. */
+#define MAX_NASTA_STA_PER_CHANNEL   64
+#define MAX_NASTA_RESPONSE_STAS     64
 
 typedef struct {
     unsigned int num_sta;
